cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the paper and the archived release."
title: "recurrent_MI: simulation code and data for mutual information in linear recurrent circuits"
abstract: >-
  Simulation code and data reproducing every figure and every number in Singh and
  Tchernookov, "Mutual information in linear recurrent circuits: inhibition in the olfactory
  bulb increases information only against a fixed noise floor". One seeded Jupyter notebook
  produces all results and checks 50 of them against the values printed in the paper.
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Vijay
    affiliation: "Department of Physics and Astronomy, Haverford College, Haverford, Pennsylvania, United States of America"
    email: vsingh1@haverford.edu
  - family-names: Tchernookov
    given-names: Martin
    affiliation: "Department of Physics, University of Wisconsin-Whitewater, Whitewater, Wisconsin, United States of America"
keywords:
  - mutual information
  - efficient coding
  - olfactory bulb
  - recurrent inhibition
  - neurogenesis
  - computational neuroscience
version: 1.0.0
